          "type": "commentary_text",
          "text": "The indicative content has been divided into four blocks of bullet points. The first block refers to how microorganisms break down the plant material. The second block refers to what is produced in this process. The third block refers to the use of the carbon dioxide produced, and the fourth block refers to the role of nitrates in the recycling process. The production of chlorophyll would be a suitable other example of the use of nitrate ions; if the student gives any other examples, please check online.",
